{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794559187178,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf096b3ffedlSFG4CQ7JPEzA","part":{"partID":"prt_1d410162b002v8CEWoMwMXxWm1","sessionID":"ses_e2bf096b3ffedlSFG4CQ7JPEzA","messageID":"msg_1d40ff11f001Dqm6Z38tWckv14","type":"tool","id":"call_ea85412eaab64013b1d1729d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md, lines 1-83\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Shared: Session Readers\"\n3: description: \"The read-only session reader package: one exact-id reader per runtime, the shared failure envelope, the capability table and the projection to the HistoryEntry list.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"session readers\"\n6:   - \"read session history\"\n7:   - \"session reader capabilities\"\n8:   - \"exact session id reader\"\n9: version: 1.0.0.0\n10: ---\n11: \n12: # Shared: Session Readers\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n17: \n18: This package reads one runtime session by its exact id and returns it as the shared `HistoryEntry` list that the history lookup core takes. It never writes. A reader opens a store read-only, proves the file or row belongs to the requested session, and returns a failure code rather than a partial list.\n19: \n20: The six decision-capture sweeps keep their own inline readers and remain the writers. Nothing here changes a save-time path.\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 2. CONTRACT\n25: \n26: - **Exact id only.** A caller names a runtime and one session id. No reader guesses the newest session or lists a store.\n27: - **Read-only.** Files are read and SQLite stores are opened with read-only flags. The side-effect suite checks that no read changes a store's bytes or modification time.\n28: - **One envelope.** `readSession` returns `{ ok: true, source, items }` or `{ ok: false, code }`. It never throws across the boundary and never returns a partial list.\n29: - **Capability is the caller's gate.** `index.mjs` exports `capabilities`, one row per runtime with its `status`, locator kind and store root, plus a `reason` when the runtime is gated. The dispatcher does not consult it. The compaction hooks and the lookup CLI check that a runtime is `ready` before they offer or read history.\n30: \n31: `loadSession` returns the raw neutral records. Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH also return `injected`, a list of `{ source, text }` for context a hook or harness put into the session, which `records` never carries. `loadSession` passes `injected` through and `readSession` ignores it, so only a caller on the raw path sees what the harness added.\n32: \n33: - Claude's `injected` source is `hook_additional_context`, one entry per hook context attachment.\n34: - Pi's `injected` source is the entry's custom type, such as `session-start-context`, or `custom_message` when it carries none.\n35: - Devin's `injected` source is `system` for a harness node and `unflagged-user` for a user node the harness wrote. The transcript fallback uses the step's own source.\n36: - DSH's `injected` source is the event's source kind, such as `repo-guards`, or `unknown` when it names none.\n37: \n38: Failure codes:\n39: \n40: | Code | Meaning |\n41: |---|---|\n42: | `locator_unavailable` | The id is empty or unsafe, or the runtime has no locator to resolve |\n43: | `capability_gated` | No reader exists for the runtime, or its switch is off |\n44: | `session_not_found` | No store record matches the id |\n45: | `session_mismatch` | A record was found, but its recorded id or path does not match |\n46: | `session_ambiguous` | More than one record claims the id |\n47: | `store_unreadable` | The store could not be read or projected |\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 3. FILES\n52: \n53: | File | Role |\n54: |---|---|\n55: | `index.mjs` | The dispatcher: `readSession` (projected entries), `loadSession` (raw records), the `capabilities` table and the failure envelope |\n56: | `identity.mjs` | Shared guards: safe session ids, path containment and the recorded-id check |\n57: | `project.mjs` | Projection from neutral records to `HistoryEntry`, with tool-call pairing |\n58: | `claude.mjs` | Claude Code transcript reader |\n59: | `codex.mjs` | Codex session log reader |\n60: | `pi.mjs` | Pi session log reader, following the live branch |\n61: | `opencode.mjs` | OpenCode SQLite store reader, which proves the session's recorded directory when the caller names one |\n62: | `devin.mjs` | Devin `sessions.db` reader over the session's main message chain and, through each compaction's `summarized_from` link, the threads before it. A recorded folder at or below the named folder passes, because Devin's hooks receive the project root. Falls back to the transcript file for a store without the session's turns |\n63: | `dsh.mjs` | DSH session log reader |\n64: | `cursor.mjs` | Cursor gate, which returns before touching any file |\n65: \n66: ---\n67: \n68: ## 4. VALIDATION\n69: \n70: From the repository root:\n71: \n72: ```bash\n73: node --test .skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/\n74: ```\n75: \n76: The matrix suite covers each runtime by store state, and the schema check validates projected entries against the history core's published JSON Schema.\n77: \n78: ---\n79: \n80: ## 5. RELATED\n81: \n82: - [`../README.md`](../README.md): the shared hook helpers this package sits beside.\n83: - [`../../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/history/README.md`](../../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/history/README.md): the lookup core and CLI that consume these readers.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md, lines 1-83\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Shared: Session Readers\"\n3: description: \"The read-only session reader package: one exact-id reader per runtime, the shared failure envelope, the capability table and the projection to the HistoryEntry list.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"session readers\"\n6:   - \"read session history\"\n7:   - \"session reader capabilities\"\n8:   - \"exact session id reader\"\n9: version: 1.0.0.0\n10: ---\n11: \n12: # Shared: Session Readers\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n17: \n18: This package reads one runtime session by its exact id and returns it as the shared `HistoryEntry` list that the history lookup core takes. It never writes. A reader opens a store read-only, proves the file or row belongs to the requested session, and returns a failure code rather than a partial list.\n19: \n20: The six decision-capture sweeps keep their own inline readers and remain the writers. Nothing here changes a save-time path.\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 2. CONTRACT\n25: \n26: - **Exact id only.** A caller names a runtime and one session id. No reader guesses the newest session or lists a store.\n27: - **Read-only.** Files are read and SQLite stores are opened with read-only flags. The side-effect suite checks that no read changes a store's bytes or modification time.\n28: - **One envelope.** `readSession` returns `{ ok: true, source, items }` or `{ ok: false, code }`. It never throws across the boundary and never returns a partial list.\n29: - **Capability is the caller's gate.** `index.mjs` exports `capabilities`, one row per runtime with its `status`, locator kind and store root, plus a `reason` when the runtime is gated. The dispatcher does not consult it. The compaction hooks and the lookup CLI check that a runtime is `ready` before they offer or read history.\n30: \n31: `loadSession` returns the raw neutral records. Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH also return `injected`, a list of `{ source, text }` for context a hook or harness put into the session, which `records` never carries. `loadSession` passes `injected` through and `readSession` ignores it, so only a caller on the raw path sees what the harness added.\n32: \n33: - Claude's `injected` source is `hook_additional_context`, one entry per hook context attachment.\n34: - Pi's `injected` source is the entry's custom type, such as `session-start-context`, or `custom_message` when it carries none.\n35: - Devin's `injected` source is `system` for a harness node and `unflagged-user` for a user node the harness wrote. The transcript fallback uses the step's own source.\n36: - DSH's `injected` source is the event's source kind, such as `repo-guards`, or `unknown` when it names none.\n37: \n38: Failure codes:\n39: \n40: | Code | Meaning |\n41: |---|---|\n42: | `locator_unavailable` | The id is empty or unsafe, or the runtime has no locator to resolve |\n43: | `capability_gated` | No reader exists for the runtime, or its switch is off |\n44: | `session_not_found` | No store record matches the id |\n45: | `session_mismatch` | A record was found, but its recorded id or path does not match |\n46: | `session_ambiguous` | More than one record claims the id |\n47: | `store_unreadable` | The store could not be read or projected |\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 3. FILES\n52: \n53: | File | Role |\n54: |---|---|\n55: | `index.mjs` | The dispatcher: `readSession` (projected entries), `loadSession` (raw records), the `capabilities` table and the failure envelope |\n56: | `identity.mjs` | Shared guards: safe session ids, path containment and the recorded-id check |\n57: | `project.mjs` | Projection from neutral records to `HistoryEntry`, with tool-call pairing |\n58: | `claude.mjs` | Claude Code transcript reader |\n59: | `codex.mjs` | Codex session log reader |\n60: | `pi.mjs` | Pi session log reader, following the live branch |\n61: | `opencode.mjs` | OpenCode SQLite store reader, which proves the session's recorded directory when the caller names one |\n62: | `devin.mjs` | Devin `sessions.db` reader over the session's main message chain and, through each compaction's `summarized_from` link, the threads before it. A recorded folder at or below the named folder passes, because Devin's hooks receive the project root. Falls back to the transcript file for a store without the session's turns |\n63: | `dsh.mjs` | DSH session log reader |\n64: | `cursor.mjs` | Cursor gate, which returns before touching any file |\n65: \n66: ---\n67: \n68: ## 4. VALIDATION\n69: \n70: From the repository root:\n71: \n72: ```bash\n73: node --test .skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/\n74: ```\n75: \n76: The matrix suite covers each runtime by store state, and the schema check validates projected entries against the history core's published JSON Schema.\n77: \n78: ---\n79: \n80: ## 5. RELATED\n81: \n82: - [`../README.md`](../README.md): the shared hook helpers this package sits beside.\n83: - [`../../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/history/README.md`](../../../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/history/README.md): the lookup core and CLI that consume these readers."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794559186475,"end":1794559187178}}}}
