{"type":"text","timestamp":1794559328743,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf096b3ffedlSFG4CQ7JPEzA","part":{"id":"prt_1d4123805002mJzwiQA3EIj96s","sessionID":"ses_e2bf096b3ffedlSFG4CQ7JPEzA","messageID":"msg_1d41223e20012j1sqKjP7KAynT","type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n**File written:** `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md`\n\nThree edits, matching T046:\n1. Added a `Contained open` bullet to §2 CONTRACT, saying each reader opens the path its containment check resolved.\n2. Extended the DSH `injected` bullet: a `user/message` with no source stays injected and never becomes a record.\n3. Changed the `store_unreadable` row in the failure-codes table to say Devin's open or projection failure falls back to the transcript first.\n\n**Verify output** (`$SRR` = the README, run from the repository root):\n\n```\n$ rg -c \"falls back to the transcript\" $SRR\n1\n$ rg -c \"with no source\" $SRR\n1\n$ rg -c \"containment check resolved\" $SRR\n1\n```\n\nAll three print 1, as T046 requires. `git status --short` for the file shows ` M` and no other file was touched by me. Checkbox left unticked.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the task says \"the Devin `store_unreadable` row\". The only row carrying that code is the shared failure-codes table row, so I scoped it there with \"For Devin, ...\". No test suite was named by this task, so none was run.","time":{"start":1794559326213,"end":1794559328743}}}
